{"author":{"id":"8d7a7fea5b07a0d5d081edd516d55afeb51ce9c18b2b2be6ceb30eb17cd9b547"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794289235,"nonce":"JPgVVdD8ttL0CrJmMndtZ2B2Vz4=","title":"Svg::stroke() has no effect on the drawn line; Svg::color() does","message":"`blinc_layout::svg::Svg::stroke(Color)` is documented as \"Set the stroke color (overrides SVG stroke without affecting fill)\". An svg whose path has `stroke=\"#00ff00\"` drawn with `.stroke(red)` stays green or is drawn in the source colour; no red pixel appears. `.color(red)` (the tint) does recolour it.\n\nMeasured (offscreen, 24x24, one path `M4 12h16`, stroke-width 4, same source for both):\n\n    .stroke(Color::rgba(1,0,0,1))   red pixels: 0\n    .color(Color::rgba(1,0,0,1))    red pixels: 64\n\nTest: crates/fs-components-fields/tests/blinc_limits.rs in FreeSynergy/fs-components, `an_svg_stroke_colour_is_drawn` (ignored until fixed; `cargo test -p fs-components-fields --test blinc_limits -- --ignored`).\n\nWorkaround in use: `.color()`. Not checked: whether `.fill()` and `.stroke_width()` have the same problem.","files":null}]}